[expect] "I want to call it “vibrations” and it belongs in cosmos.   It’s hard to appreciate how everything really everything is made up of vibrations, that is, disturbances that propagate  We tend to think of vibrations through the chart of a sign wave or other wave forms in two dimensions one is time and the other is something moving up and down    But something moved up and down in three dimensions so vibrations are four dimensional    Also, we tend to think of vibrations as repeating, like a sign wave or a wheel turning. Indeed it’s easy to see how a wheel turning is what produces a sine wave.  But waves come in all shapes and they change dynamically, and those changes are information. The sound of a tree falling in the forest is different from the sound of a bird chirping or your heart beating when you’re still.  And it’s different from the color of the bird are the warmth of your heart.    When you drop a pebble in a still pond, it pushes the water away that's a single ring moving into dimensions. It's a circle. You don't see it moving in the third dimension down into the water, but that's happening too. and because the water is compressible. It pushes back up. And makes another ring, and takes a while to settle. If you drop two stones in the Stillpond, both will make waves, and the waves will cross each other and interfere, making a beautiful pattern If you drop two stones in the Stillpond, both will make waves and the waves will cross each other and interfere making a beautiful pattern.    In a concert hall with 60 instruments playing, there are complex vibrations emerging in three dimensions from each instrument. We are complex vibrations, emerging in three dimensions from each instrument, and varying with the quality of the instrument, bouncing off the walls. Interfering and reinforcing one another. Like a crystalline, gossamer web. If you’re sensitive, your ears pick up subtle differences that let you not only identify what instruments are playing, but where they’re coming from.  ((I realize the inspiration I had earlier is fading and I don’t remember what I really wanted to talk about. I’m tired. I'll get back to this later.))"
